{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental","id":1085961,"title":"System for healing non-magical diseases and illnesses (whether physical or mental)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-30T17:37:31-07:00","id":1085961,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> System for healing non-magical diseases and illnesses (whether physical or mental)?","content":"Specifically I am interested in the possibility of, and means by which a mage would go about healing diseases of non-magical origin of whatever kind, whether caused by bacteria, viruses, genetic abnormalities, <i>whatever</i>: AIDS/HIV, ebola, bubonic plague, Crohn's, cancer (any/all cancer), Rhett syndrome (look it up and be horrified), Parkinson's, ALS, Alzheimer's, etc. On the mental side, I'd like to know how to cure things like PTSD, phobias, bipolar disorder, and other derangements of non-magical origin such as people acquire and live with in the real world. For the purposes of this conversation, let us assume the truth of the mind/body distinction.<br /> <br /> <b>Diseases/Illnesses of the &quot;Body&quot;</b><br /> <br /> I am familiar with the oft-cited chart regarding &quot;Toxin&quot;-rating and what have you, which is used to determine the game system effects of being inflicted with one or more of these conditions, and certainly I would imagine that any system that involves utterly ridding a person's body of such a diseasewould ideally involve that chart (because it represents the authors' creation of a metric by which to gauge the relative &quot;badness&quot; of each malady)--but I have yet to find concrete system for permanently treating these things and ridding them from the patient for good. For reference, I have looked at every edition of the main core book (first edition through M20, as well as Sorcerer's Crusade; though admittedly I skipped <i>Dark Ages: Mage</i> on the grounds that its magic system is so different from the other editions that it probably wouldn't be instructive or useful to me); both editions of the Verbena tradition book (the Rev. edition of which I believe has one the best and deepest treatment of the systems associated with the use of Life for various purposes including healing and permanently altering a subject in a variety of ways); <i>The Guide to the Traditions</i>; The <i>Guide to the Technocracy</i>; both editions of the Progenitors convention book; <i>The Book of Shadows</i>; <i>Master's of the Arts</i>; and <i>How Do You Do That</i>?. And for all that searching I've have little or nothing. Zero. Nada. At best I know it's tough, and <i>probably</i> involves an extended roll (maybe?), and depending on how you read different sources together, I could make arguments of various strengths for different diseases potentially being curable at Life 2, Life 3, or Life 4 depending on a variety of factors ranging from how &quot;bad&quot; they are, to what causes them--e.g., I would potentially argue that curing a bacterial infection is easier than curing a genetic defect, in that curing a bacterial infection merely requires ridding the host of the harmful microorganisms in question, whereas a genetic disease like Rhett or Huntington's may well constitute a permanent alteration to someone's DNA/pattern.<br /> <br /> And yet there's no guidance on how long it would take to cure someone of any one these. Sure something things are gimmees: structural problems for instance. <i>Verbena </i>(Rev.) talks about correcting birth defects as being treated as a &quot;permanent enhancement&quot; and refers the reader to that system and section of that book accordingly. With that in mind, I would obviously modify that stated system such that, in the instance of correcting a congenital defect, I would not require the beneficiary of the healing/modification to endure a permanent point of paradox because, ultimately, there is nothing inherently vulgar about <i>not </i>having a cleft palate, or polydactyly, or <i>not </i>having a bicuspid aorta (we're supposed to have tri-cuspid aortic valves). These are structural alterations not dissimilar from adding fangs, a tail, or claws... except that you're going from one state of coincidental existence to another (rather than turning from a human into a wombat-inspired crinos for or whatever).<br /> <br /> But can a Mage with Life 3 or 4 just wave their hand and cure Parkinson's? or AIDS/HIV? I am reminded of the scene from <i>Star Trek IV</i> when they're in the hospital and Dr. Bones is continually confronted with situations in which he basically has a pill or relatively quick fix for <i>everything</i>. Without getting into deeper meta-gaming discussions about, &quot;well, if they can just wave their hand, why don't they blah blah blah&quot;, what's a fair, and internally systematically consistent way of handling these sorts of workings?<br /> <br /> <b>Diseases/Illnesses of the &quot;Mind&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The same question goes for various levels of Mind (and potentially Life as well I suppose), and the means by which we could cure people of PTSD (which specifically M20 says is possible, though hints at it being not easy), being bipolar schizophrenic, or any one of a number of derangements? Keep in mind I'm not trying to heal Malkavians, metises, Silver Fangs, other Garou in harano--nobody who has a mental, psychological, or emotional condition by dint of a supernatural force acting upon them (such as a curse or whatever). I'm talking about conditions such as the ones mentioned that occur naturally, via the processes and mechanism by which such things typically occur.<br /> <br /> Any help of guidance people would like to provide would be helpful--though I would point out that I'm not looking for avoidances--i.e., responses to the question that avoid the problem presented by declaring that perhaps the question is invalid in the first place because these games don't have to/shouldn't be reduced down to dice/rolling/whate-have-you. I can appreciate that some people have a jolly ol' time coming up with the how hard something is to do on the fly, with every instance of a thing being different to the last according to the narrative needs of the particular situation--but for the purposes of this quandry, we should assume that that approach has been examined, considered, and specifically rejected in favor of having a concrete system that operates in a consistent manner regardless of its tendency to either enhance or diffuse the drama of a given story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 04-30-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:26:20-07:00","id":1086694,"title":"","content":"The major reason that mages can't (in the Modern Era) go around healing people willy-nilly is because of Paradox and Consensus. While people &quot;want&quot; to be cured/healed, Reality(tm) is still structured around much of their negativity and self-deceit. Also, it's important to keep in mind that in the WoD, things are darker/bleaker than in our Real World(tm). While many/most(?) STs likely just use the real-world elements as-is, unlike in our world the WoD has *active* agents (mages, spirits, etc.) who *promote* disease/pain/suffering. HIV -- just to use that as an example -- isn't &quot;simply&quot; HIV in the WoD -- it's a disease which has spirits (mostly Middle Umbral, but some who are Low Umbral and a few High Umbral as well) that *support* its existence, and take active steps (when and where they can, which isn't always but often enough) to perpetuate the disease (having it adapt/resist treatment in a way that is beyond what occurs in real life). Same goes for a number of other things, too.<br /> <br /> A given mage with the right paradigm can heal any given *individual* of, say, HIV or severe PTSD (using Life:3 for the former, and Mind:3-4 for the latter, depending on certain salient aspects), but said mage (or even group of mages) would be hard-pressed to heal a hospital ward of afflicted individuals, and finding an as-yet-&quot;unaccepted&quot; cure for those things on a global scale is to face Paradox, directly. Mages lose. Period. Only the gradual, slow shifting of Paradigm/Consensus would allow for such things to be more globally treated... and that element is tied to the very underpinnings of what Mage/the WoD is literally all about.<br /> <br /> (Sidenote: I've got a character I've played on-and-off for many years now -- since the old, original forum days of the 90s -- who has been trying to slowly work towards a cure for HIV via gradual Consensus-shifting and attacking &quot;Paradox&quot; via having multiple papers published by different doctors/research groups in hopes of shifting the world paradigm enough to allow is already-long-existing &quot;cure&quot; (Life:3, which for him is the Pillar -- Biometabolics:3) to be more globally accepted. It's been two decades, both in real life and in-game. Still working on it...)<br /> <br /> So, much like with shooting a fireball from their magic wand or hypnotizing a given individual with a pendant or crystal, any given mage *can* just &quot;waive their hand&quot;, as it were, and do &quot;x&quot;; but just like with said fireball or mind control/alteration, Paradox may have something to say about it... and even if not in the short term, then in the long-run via Disbelief and other forces working to sustain the negative forces in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:01:17-07:00","id":1086730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086694#post1086694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While many/most(?) STs likely just use the real-world elements as-is, unlike in our world the WoD has *active* agents (mages, spirits, etc.) who *promote* disease/pain/suffering. HIV -- just to use that as an example -- isn't &quot;simply&quot; HIV in the WoD -- it's a disease which has spirits (mostly Middle Umbral, but some who are Low Umbral and a few High Umbral as well) that *support* its existence, and take active steps (when and where they can, which isn't always but often enough) to perpetuate the disease (having it adapt/resist treatment in a way that is beyond what occurs in real life). Same goes for a number of other things, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that in your interpretation of the WoD, behind every individual presentation of a given disease or illness, there is a spiritual agent actively promoting the growth and spread of the disease specifically within the person so afflicted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086694#post1086694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A given mage with the right paradigm can heal any given *individual* of, say, HIV or severe PTSD (using Life:3 for the former, and Mind:3-4 for the latter, depending on certain salient aspects)</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. I'm not really concerned with doing an entire hospital ward, really--I just want to know what if any process is for doing one person. How long does it take? What are the circumstances that make the roll harder or easier (whether by shifting actual diff. number, or by requiring a success threshold)? And I'm also interested in why you specifically chose Life 3 for curing HIV (does this also go for cancer, lupus, ALS, Crohn's, Huntington's, Parkinson's, Alzheimer's?), and what your rationale is for Mind 3-4 for curing PTSD.<br /> <br /> I mean, is this nitty gritty written about or discussed <i>anywhere </i>in WW canon? These are pretty human problems common to people the world over (who here has <i>not </i>wished they could cure themselves or a loved one of a debilitating illness or condition?), you'd think that they would have dressed the inevitably scenario of a Mage trying to cure their wife/husband/child of Xyz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:58:27-07:00","id":1086751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. I'm not really concerned with doing an entire hospital ward, really--I just want to know what if any process is for doing one person. How long does it take? What are the circumstances that make the roll harder or easier (whether by shifting actual diff. number, or by requiring a success threshold)? And I'm also interested in why you specifically chose Life 3 for curing HIV (does this also go for cancer, lupus, ALS, Crohn's, Huntington's, Parkinson's, Alzheimer's?), and what your rationale is for Mind 3-4 for curing PTSD.<br /> <br /> I mean, is this nitty gritty written about or discussed <i>anywhere </i>in WW canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite simply, what you're looking for it's the basic rules of magick + the Sphere descriptions.<br /> <br /> Sphere magick isn't just rotes and concrete systems, you need to read and interpret. What Jhon says it's mostly common sense (applied to lore).<br /> <br /> Why Life 3? Because Life 3 &quot;heals others&quot;any diease would be cured at this level becasue healing a diease it's healing other. Curing a congenital diease it's different because the diease &quot;it's part of the Pattern of the individual&quot; (you can heal the body to it's &quot;healty state&quot;, but if you were born with an ill, it is your &quot;natural healty state&quot;), so you can argue for that being a little more difficult (albeit it's debatable).<br /> <br /> Why Mind 3-4? Because a mental ilness it's usualy regarded as something rooted within the deepts of your mind, with Mind 3 you can read the subconscious mind and imprint suggestions within it (as per social conditioning). But it can be argued that you need Mind 4 to just wave your hand and heal the condition because Mind 4 allows to trully control the mind (Mind 3 would be more a push on the right direction). Mind 5 may be overkill because it allows to rebuild the whole mind, but you could make a case for curing deep insanity being Mind 5 (the same level that allows to reconstruct the Nature).<br /> <br /> The minimum time that it takes, the difficulty, and other stuff are determined by the basic rules of magic as well...and you're encouragerd to modify these according the Paradigm of the Mage (I.E, some mages favor the ritual stuff and may take longer than a handwave).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-02-2017, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:42:35-07:00","id":1086767,"title":"","content":"I think personally that I might require a little bit of Life as well, when it comes to healing mental illness. A lot of mental illness is chemical or hormonal after all, and even things like trauma have an effect on the physical structure of the brain. But I'm not married to that idea.<br /> <br /> (It would be interesting actually to deal with a character whose conception of the world involved the idea that mental illness was demonic possession. Would they then be able to exorcise the &quot;demon&quot; with spirit or prime? I admit, I lean toward no, myself. But it's rather fun to think about.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  I clearly needed to read the original post more closely, sorry. 05-02-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:46:38-07:00","id":1086804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086767#post1086767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think personally that I might require a little bit of Life as well, when it comes to healing mental illness. A lot of mental illness is chemical or hormonal after all, and even things like trauma have an effect on the physical structure of the brain. But I'm not married to that idea.<br /> <br /> (It would be interesting actually to deal with a character whose conception of the world involved the idea that mental illness was demonic possession. Would they then be able to exorcise the &quot;demon&quot; with spirit or prime? I admit, I lean toward no, myself. But it's rather fun to think about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point--but would the metaphysics of the game and sphere magic(k) necessarily be beholden to what we IRL recognize to be the foundational principles of life science? perhaps a Technocrat might need to use a conjunctional Life+Mind effect to help someone with schizophrenia, but a Verbena or Dreamspeaker might just need Mind (hell, the Dreamspeaker might also need Spirit in that case).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:10:46-07:00","id":1086824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086804#post1086804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair point--but would the metaphysics of the game and sphere magic(k) necessarily be beholden to what we IRL recognize to be the foundational principles of life science? perhaps a Technocrat might need to use a conjunctional Life+Mind effect to help someone with schizophrenia, but a Verbena or Dreamspeaker might just need Mind (hell, the Dreamspeaker might also need Spirit in that case).</div> </div> </div> </div>That probably will be dependent on how exactly you, as storyteller, define the consensus. If you define fairly established modern medical knowledge as part of the consensus, then there is at least an an argument that it should be a combination of Life and Mind. Your players may be able to make an argument as to why, based on their paradigm and conception of magic, that one or the other might not be necessary.<br /> <br /> I admit, I'd probably lean toward Life+Mind as default, and then decide based on how well the players sell me on their argument.<br /> <br /> For something like a chronic physical or mental illness, I probably would allow the characters to cure it permanently, but it wouldn't be a &quot;wave of a hand&quot; kind of deal. I would definitely require an extended ritual and multiple successes. Not necessarily all at once, but maybe something with regular monthly treatment for a year or something. I think I'd consider curing all of the diseases and ailments you mention as a Life 3 sort of deal, but I would use difficulty and amount of successes to regulate what I personally think the difficulty will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:35:21-07:00","id":1087717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086730#post1086730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that in your interpretation of the WoD, behind every individual presentation of a given disease or illness, there is a spiritual agent actively promoting the growth and spread of the disease specifically within the person so afflicted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhmmm... well... *no*. That is, it's not &quot;my interpretation&quot; of the setting -- that's actually *a part* of the setting of WoD (both in Mage and in Werewolf). There are spiritual essences behind virtually everything in the WoD. Some are more passive, some more active, some can work their power/essence directly while others have to wait for opportune moments and/or times when the Gauntlet/Shroud thins... but that's how things run in WoD, per the books. Now that doesn't mean that *everything* is caused or directly influenced by a given spirit (or set of spirits) 24/7/365 -- there are plenty of mundane influences, as well, at work causing this, that and the other to happen for perfectly &quot;ordinary&quot; reasons -- but when talking about Mage(tm) (and Werewolf(tm), and sometimes other pieces of the WoD pie, depending on circumstances), it *is* something that the PCs/ST has to keep in mind when trying to do &quot;x&quot; in many situations. That's what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1086730#post1086730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. I'm not really concerned with doing an entire hospital ward, really--I just want to know what if any process is for doing one person. How long does it take? What are the circumstances that make the roll harder or easier (whether by shifting actual diff. number, or by requiring a success threshold)? And I'm also interested in why you specifically chose Life 3 for curing HIV (does this also go for cancer, lupus, ALS, Crohn's, Huntington's, Parkinson's, Alzheimer's?), and what your rationale is for Mind 3-4 for curing PTSD.<br /> <br /> I mean, is this nitty gritty written about or discussed <i>anywhere </i>in WW canon? These are pretty human problems common to people the world over (who here has <i>not </i>wished they could cure themselves or a loved one of a debilitating illness or condition?), you'd think that they would have dressed the inevitably scenario of a Mage trying to cure their wife/husband/child of Xyz.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's very little nitty-gritty when it comes to this, and there never was really relative to the different editions of WoD/Mage. There are guidelines and &quot;ratings&quot; for diseases/poisons/what-have-you (which you can find in the core books/ST guides), and things like &quot;How long does it take?&quot;, etc., are largely dependent on (P)aradigm and methodologies used. That is, it isn't necessarily that one particular way is &quot;right&quot; or &quot;correct&quot; more so than others (though those that violate Consensus(tm) less often are more effective in the long run), but rather that some game mechanics coupled with applied common sense can go a long way. <br /> <br /> Examples: a faith healer might be able to rid a person of HIV within just a few brief moments of prayer (and a good number of successes/Q and WP spent); said healing may be &quot;permanent&quot;, of it might merely temporarily suppress the disease/infection until if/when Disbelief or looming Paradox comes crashing down (which is only determinable by ST judgement -- how well documented/&quot;known&quot; is the victim's having of the disease? -- how aware is Reality(tm) of his having it? How many successes did the healer roll (representing the amount of faith/divine power was channeled through to make the healing &quot;stick&quot;)? All of those things are factors. Alternately, a more science-minded mage may treat the patient with various chemicals and/or natural derivatives over a course of months or even years (building successes gradually over a period of time). Coupled with the patient perhaps changing his life -- moving, not necessarily being near/in contact with people who know/knew of the infection, creating effectively a &quot;new life&quot; for himself -- the &quot;spell&quot; may take quite some time to &quot;cast&quot; (much longer than the few moments of the faith healer), but because of (P)aradigm, technique, and over-arcing factors related to Consensus, the curing of the particular patient may in fact be permanent and perhaps even without looming Paradox floating about.<br /> <br /> The solutions you are looking for -- in the manner in which you're asking -- aren't really what Mage(tm) is founded on, both mechanically, metaphysically and narratively. There are ways and ways and ways again in which &quot;x&quot; can often be accomplished, and in different ways with different means that can affect time involved, magic (read: Spheres) involved, as well as how Paradoxical said workings can be. There is no single (or simple) answer to what you're asking. And that's why Mage(tm) is more &quot;magic(k)al&quot; than most other game systems/settings: half of it exists outside the context of &quot;mundane rules&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T19:38:53-07:00","id":1090093,"title":"","content":"I'll add my voice to the chorus of &quot;Life 3/Mind 4 with a relatively high number of successes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:49:19-07:00","id":1090303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalinara</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think personally that I might require a little bit of Life as well, when it comes to healing mental illness. A lot of mental illness is chemical or hormonal after all, and even things like trauma have an effect on the physical structure of the brain. But I'm not married to that idea.<br /> <br /> (It would be interesting actually to deal with a character whose conception of the world involved the idea that mental illness was demonic possession. Would they then be able to exorcise the &quot;demon&quot; with spirit or prime? I admit, I lean toward no, myself. But it's rather fun to think about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I mean, I can see the argument in many cases, but I have a more psychoanalytic background and I believe in trauma being cured with good old &quot;couch sessions&quot;, if you get what I mean, without needing more violent biological approaches.<br /> <br /> I could argue with the rules and say that, well, with Mind 5 you can create a whole disembodied mind (nothing says that you can't include traumas)...so you can put in doubt the notion that the &quot;the mind it's in the brain&quot;. Which could be countered saying that, well, the Consensus says the brain it's the home of the mind, so it is.<br /> I think it's debatable.<br /> <br /> I think I would lean for Mind 4 for some cases (those that don't need a chemical or invasive treatment in real life) and Mind 4/Life 3 OR Mind 5 for the most severe problems (arguing that the Consensus allows for a break for those that believe in the importance of the brain...as long as they can alter it too).<br /> <br /> About Spirit...my first answer would be no. Otherwise Spirit mages would need/use Spirit for everything. I may allow it to replace Life, however. Maybe the rote could be Spirit 4/Mind 4 to expell the bad spirits from the spiritual landscape of the mind of the subject (there's not much about entering the minds of people...but you can enter the spiritual landscape of dreams with Mind 3. Maybe you can access the subconscious too?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-09-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:19:01-07:00","id":1090378,"title":"","content":"I'm having an issue formulating a response to you because, to my eyes at least, you look to have taken a somewhat inconsistent position on a material issue relating to this topic. Specifically: whether every individual presentation of a disease or illness within any given person brings with it a concomitant, individual spiritual entity specific to that particular person and their specific presentation of that disease or illness.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that my original statement was (pertinently): &quot;<i>So you're saying that in your interpretation of the WoD, <b>behind every individual presentation of a given disease or illness, there is a spiritual agent actively promoting the growth and spread of the disease specifically within the person so afflicted?</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Here you appear to take the position that this <i>is</i> the case, and what's more, that there is such textual support for this position that no reasonable person could determine otherwise (emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1087717#post1087717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhmmm... well... *no*. That is, it's not &quot;my interpretation&quot; of the setting -- <b>that's actually *a part* of the setting of WoD (both in Mage and in Werewolf)</b>. There are spiritual essences behind virtually everything in the WoD. Some are more passive, some more active, some can work their power/essence directly while others have to wait for opportune moments and/or times when the Gauntlet/Shroud thins... <b>but that's how things run in WoD, per the books</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My confusion stems from the remainder of that paragraph, because it seems to take a difference position from what I just quoted; to wit: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1087717#post1087717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now <b>that doesn't mean that *everything* is caused or directly influenced by a given spirit</b> (or set of spirits) 24/7/365 -- there are plenty of mundane influences, as well, at work causing this, that and the other to happen for perfectly &quot;ordinary&quot; reasons -- but when talking about Mage(tm) (and Werewolf(tm), and sometimes other pieces of the WoD pie, depending on circumstances), <b>it *is* something that the PCs/ST has to keep in mind when trying to do &quot;x&quot; in many situations.</b> That's what I was saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is much more akin to what I thought: i.e., that if I get [insert disease], there isn't necessarily a [insert disease] spirit hovering around me in the umbra correlated to the individualized presence of the disease or illness in my body--but that it <i>could</i> be the case under certain circumstances (or perhaps that there might be one big [insert disease] spirit for an entire floor of a hospital dedicated to people suffering from [insert disease].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1087717#post1087717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's very little nitty-gritty when it comes to this, and there never was really relative to the different editions of WoD/Mage. There are guidelines and &quot;ratings&quot; for diseases/poisons/what-have-you (which you can find in the core books/ST guides), and things like &quot;How long does it take?&quot;, etc., are largely dependent on (P)aradigm and methodologies used. That is, it isn't necessarily that one particular way is &quot;right&quot; or &quot;correct&quot; more so than others (though those that violate Consensus(tm) less often are more effective in the long run), but rather that some game mechanics coupled with applied common sense can go a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine--I just wanted to make sure there wasn't a system or rule of any kind specific to these circumstances before I made my ruling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:32:00-07:00","id":1095717,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late response -- been very busy with business and traveling, so haven't been on for a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085961-system-for-healing-non-magical-diseases-and-illnesses-whether-physical-or-mental?p=1090378#post1090378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having an issue formulating a response to you because, to my eyes at least, you look to have taken a somewhat inconsistent position on a material issue relating to this topic. Specifically: whether every individual presentation of a disease or illness within any given person brings with it a concomitant, individual spiritual entity specific to that particular person and their specific presentation of that disease or illness.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that my original statement was (pertinently): &quot;<i>So you're saying that in your interpretation of the WoD, <b>behind every individual presentation of a given disease or illness, there is a spiritual agent actively promoting the growth and spread of the disease specifically within the person so afflicted?</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Here you appear to take the position that this <i>is</i> the case, and what's more, that there is such textual support for this position that no reasonable person could determine otherwise (emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My confusion stems from the remainder of that paragraph, because it seems to take a difference position from what I just quoted; to wit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is much more akin to what I thought: i.e., that if I get [insert disease], there isn't necessarily a [insert disease] spirit hovering around me in the umbra correlated to the individualized presence of the disease or illness in my body--but that it <i>could</i> be the case under certain circumstances (or perhaps that there might be one big [insert disease] spirit for an entire floor of a hospital dedicated to people suffering from [insert disease].<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's fine--I just wanted to make sure there wasn't a system or rule of any kind specific to these circumstances before I made my ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps my phrasing was a bit off, but I don't see where there should have been any significant confusion. There *are* spirits of disease, and they are usually present (if sometimes dormantly so) pretty much everywhere (just as there are spirits for most all things about... pretty much everywhere). My additional point about not *everything* being influenced 24/7/365 by spirits is that there are instances wherein a (for example) dormant spirit/metaphysical presence may be about but not necessarily *directly* influencing things, but merely &quot;present&quot; due to the existence of &quot;x&quot; in the physical world. As a general rule of thumb/guideline, though, if one is trying to eradicate a disease (that is, cure it permanently and effectively remove its Pattern from existence), you're going to run head-long into opposing the spirit(s) of disease (the one, in particular, and likely other spirits of disease, as well). Even when trying to heal an individual, it simply depends on the circumstances; that's why I cited the examples I did in my response. There are no &quot;fixed&quot; time tables nor listing for successes required to do &quot;x&quot; because it really and truly &quot;depends&quot; -- on Paradigm, on the specific methodologies used, on the overarching Consensus and how Paradoxical the healing might be, etc. and et al....<br /> <br /> Generally, healing a simple cold would likely only take 2 successes (relative to healing a given uncomplicated wound); healing a systemically harmful but otherwise vulnerable disease (like HIV, which is dangerous within a host body but comparatively vulnerable relative to many diseases when outside of one) could take as little as, say, 3 successes for a same-night infection to 5-10+ for a years-long infected (and having developed AIDS) target; healing a target of genetically-prone disease (such as cancer which is intrinsic to their Pattern vs. being induced from environmental conditions) is actually more difficult, comparatively, as the &quot;healing&quot; requires permanently altering the target's genes/Life Pattern... or else the disease will simply recur after being cured (10+ successes for a &quot;permanent&quot; cure, though in that context Life:3/Entropy:4 can cut the number of successes required down as Entropy helps mitigate the likelihood of the cancer recurring whether innately or by external sources).<br /> <br /> Those are ballpark figures, and they don't go into the nuances of when &quot;x&quot; can simply be handled with a few successes vs. when they require 20+ -- along with some Willpower and Quintessence -- because there are simply too many bases to cover. ST judgement goes a long way here, as the specifics will vary from target-to-target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}